silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_03_free_monad_unpacked_sections_01_polynomial_endofunctor_concrete_anchor_3#orientationsourcesignature silm:hasLongDescription "The OrientationSourceSignature is the typed source signature (sorts Witness, TypedLeg, Apex, Profile, Render, Validation; operations cite, type, glue, profile, render, validate). In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'Sigma', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
